[KiCad-IOS port] kiway.h: select LIB_ENV_VAR by OS, not by wx port

LIB_ENV_VAR was chosen by wx port macro: __WXMAC__ -> DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH.
Under the wxQt port __WXMAC__ is never defined, even on macOS/iOS, so
every translation unit including kiway.h hit "#error Platform support
missing" (37 diagnostics in the desktop wxQt catalogue — the single
largest error class). The loader variable is a property of the host
OS, so test __APPLE__ (defined by the compiler on macOS and iOS for
every wx port) instead. No behaviour change for wxMSW/wxGTK/wxOSX.

Modified file (GPL-3.0-or-later, same license as upstream):
  include/kiway.h

--- a/include/kiway.h
+++ b/include/kiway.h
@@ -117,7 +117,11 @@
 #ifndef SWIG
 #if defined(__linux__) || defined(__FreeBSD__)
  #define LIB_ENV_VAR    wxT( "LD_LIBRARY_PATH" )
-#elif defined(__WXMAC__)
+#elif defined(__APPLE__)
+ // [KiCad-IOS port] Test the OS, not the wx port: under wxQt __WXMAC__
+ // is never defined (the port is __WXQT__), so the old test fell into
+ // the #error below on Apple hosts. __APPLE__ covers macOS and iOS
+ // for every wx port.
  #define LIB_ENV_VAR    wxT( "DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH" )
 #elif defined(_WIN32)
  #define LIB_ENV_VAR    wxT( "PATH" )
